# Frontend build context exclusions.
#
# Docker reads .dockerignore only from the build context root. The frontend
# image is built with the frontend/ directory as its context, so this file
# governs it. Before this file existed the root .dockerignore was silently
# ignored for that build, and the whole working tree was sent as context,
# including host build artifacts that can mask a broken build.

# Dependencies are installed inside the image by `npm ci`.
node_modules

# Build output, recreated inside the image by `npm run build`.
dist

# Vite/Vitest caches.
.vite

# TypeScript incremental build cache. A stale cache makes `tsc -b` consider the
# project up to date and skip the type check, which hides real type errors and
# was the mechanism behind a CI failure that appeared green locally.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Files emitted next to the source by the composite `tsconfig.node.json` build.
# Vite resolves vite.config.js before vite.config.ts, so a stale emitted sibling
# would silently take precedence over the real configuration. The TypeScript
# source (vite.config.ts) is intentionally kept.
vite.config.js
vite.config.d.ts

# Local logs.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
